# API conventions

- All routes under `/api/v1/`. Version explicitly.
- DRF ViewSets + serializers + routers for CRUD.
- Auth: JWT (simplejwt) or OAuth2. Every endpoint requires auth except explicitly
  public reads (public feed, guidebook browse).
- Object-level permission classes mapped to roles: Admin, City Founder,
  Team Member (read-only subset per FR 185), Member, Non-Member.
- Cursor pagination for feeds/lists (not offset).
- Validate ALL input via serializers. Never trust client-computed eligibility/results.
- Keep views thin — delegate to services/selectors.

# OpenAPI docs (drf-spectacular)

Every new API endpoint MUST appear in Swagger UI (`/api/v1/docs/` when enabled).

- Wire routes in the app's `urls.py` and include from `config/urls.py`.
- ViewSets: set `serializer_class`; add `@extend_schema` / `@extend_schema_view` when
  actions need custom summary, tags, or non-obvious request/response shapes.
- `APIView` / function views: MUST use `@extend_schema` with `tags`, `summary`, and
  typed `request` / `responses` serializers.
- Reuse serializers for OpenAPI types; add dedicated schema-only serializers when
  response shape differs from write serializers.
- Use tags matching the app/domain (`accounts`, `tenancy`, `events`, …). Add new tags
  to `SPECTACULAR_SETTINGS["TAGS"]` in `config/settings/base.py` when introducing a
  new bounded context.
- Document auth requirements (`auth=[]` for public endpoints) and error responses where
  non-standard.
- After adding endpoints, verify they show up at `/api/v1/docs/` (local/dev only;
  disabled in prod via `API_DOCS_ENABLED`).
